    "long_instructions": "# Modify: Check Before You Move\r\n\r\nYour Task: A painter is painting a path in front of the food truck. Right now, the program tells the Painter to keep moving after the last square, so it runs into the planter. Make the program handle the end of the path, and turn the Painter to face the truck.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the program. What happens at the end of the path? Read the error message.\r\n2. Add an `if` so the Painter only moves when `can_move()` is True. Run it again. Does the error go away? Which way is the Painter facing?\r\n3. Add an `else` branch that turns the Painter to face the food truck.\r\n4. Use Validate to check your work.\r\n\r\nCoding Tip: The Painter faces east, and the truck is south of the path. The setup lines turned the Painter right once. How did they do it?",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\n# Painter setup: these lines restock the Painter and move it to the start of the path.\nmove()\ntake_paint()\ntake_paint()\ntake_paint()\ntake_paint()\nmove()\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nmove()\nturn_left()\n\n# Your code goes below\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
